    "A fire broke out in the residential area of Jembatan Besi 1, Tambora, West Jakarta, late on Monday evening.",
    "The blaze resulted in the destruction of 75 structures, including homes and rented units, affecting approximately 400 residents.",
    "Initial reports indicate the incident caused injuries to three people and authorities suspect the cause was an electrical short circuit."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The fire incident occurred on November 23, 2026, around 10:04 PM WIB in the densely populated neighborhood of Jembatan Besi 1, located in the Tambora district of West Jakarta. According to reports from the field, the fire spread rapidly through the area, consuming a total of 75 buildings, which comprised both private residences and rental housing units. Local officials and emergency services responded to the scene to manage the situation. While the exact circumstances are still under investigation, preliminary findings by authorities suggest that the fire originated from an electrical short circuit. The event has caused significant displacement, with an estimated 400 people impacted by the loss of their homes and property. Additionally, emergency services confirmed that three individuals sustained injuries during the disaster. Recovery efforts are currently being coordinated to assist those affected by the loss of their housing.",
